# The documented commands checked against the live Herdr and Treehouse CLIs
#
# The dispatch recipe is only safe if the flags it prescribes exist and mean
# what the recipe assumes. These are the real tools installed on this machine.


== herdr agent prompt --help (the hazard the recipe now bounds) ==
      --wait
          Wait for the first matching state observed after submission

      --until <STATUS>
          State to match after --wait; repeat for more than one state
          
          [possible values: idle, working, blocked, done, unknown]

      --timeout <MS>
          Fail after this many milliseconds

When submission starts from a non-working state, --wait first requires an observed state change within 5000ms; otherwise it returns agent_prompt_stalled. A shorter --timeout returns timeout instead. It then matches idle, done, or blocked by default, or any exact --until state. It does not track turns: if the agent is already working, that active turn's completion may match. Without --timeout, the settled-state wait is indefinite.



== herdr agent wait --help ==
      --timeout <MS>
          Fail after this many milliseconds

Without --until, matches idle, done, or blocked. Use --until unknown explicitly when needed. Without --timeout, waits indefinitely.



== treehouse get --help ==
Flags:
  -h, --help                  help for get
      --json                  Print lease allocation as JSON (requires --lease)
      --lease                 Durably lease a worktree without opening a subshell; print only its path to stdout
      --lease-holder string   Optional label recorded as the lease holder (defaults to $TREEHOUSE_LEASE_HOLDER)


== treehouse return --help ==
Flags:
      --force                    Clean, reset, and return without prompting
  -h, --help                     help for return
      --if-lease-holder string   Return only if the current lease has this holder
      --if-lease-id string       Return only if the current lease has this identity


== the pane-closure predicate the recipe uses, evaluated against the live pane list ==
jq expression taken from close_pane in docs/dispatch.md:
  any(.result.panes[]; .pane_id == $pane)

live pane ids reported by "herdr pane list": wM:p1P wM:p5M wM:p5P wX:pP wX:p2B wX:p2N wH:p1A wH:p1D wH:p1K wW:p4 wW:p11 wY:p1
predicate for a live pane (wM:p1P): true
predicate for a pane that is not open (wZ:p7): false

A closed pane therefore reports false, which is exactly the condition
close_pane requires before the recipe returns a Treehouse lease.
